  "prefLabel": "Env-A 4602.65 Recordation",
  "priorExpiration": "2009-03-30",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 4602.65 “Recordation” means, with regard to CO2 allowances, the movement of CO2 allowances by the regional organization from one CO2 allowance tracking system account to another, for purposes of allocation, transfer, or deduction. The term includes “record” when used as a verb and “recorded” as appropriate.\n\nSource. #9283, INTERIM, eff 10-1-08, EXPIRED: 3-30-09\n\nNew. #9444, eff 4-3-09; ss by #10468, eff 1-1-14 (from Env-A 4602.61); ss by #12967, eff 1-1-20 (from Env-A 4602.67)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a4600.html"
